      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of the polar curve $r=-2.5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ?$",
      "worked_solution": "The polar equation $r=2a\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ defines a circle of radius $|a|$ centered at the point $(0,a).$\n\nIn our case, we have $r=-2.5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and therefore\n\n$$\na=\\frac{(-2.5)}{2}=-1.25.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $r=-2.5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ gives a circle of radius $|-1.25|=1.25$ centered at the point $(0,-1.25),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253930/assets/617b3bbebdad974775ba5dd063066d590a759db74f97260816618b5220c7221e.png)",
